# This example shows the forced first interaction mode 
# (edited by Andrea Frassà, 11/10/26)
#
# The first interaction of each primary gamma of the source MyForcedSource is 
# forced to be a photo absorption (PHOT). The interaction point is sampled from
# sigma_PHOT(x) * exp(-integral sigma_total) along the straight path of the photon,
# i.e. it is where a real first photo absorption would be. All following 
# interactions (and all secondaries) are analog.
# Allowed values: COMP, PHOT, PAIR, RAYL
#
# Each forced event contains a comment line:
# CC ForcedFirstInteraction <PrimaryID> <Forced> <OK|FAILED> <Weight>
# with Weight = probability that the first interaction of this photon is of the forced type


# Global parameters:
Version               1
Geometry              $(MEGALIB)/resource/examples/geomega/special/Spheric.geo.setup

# Physics list
PhysicsListEM                        LivermorePol

# Output formats
StoreSimulationInfo                  all



# Run: 10 MeV narrow beam (radius 1 mm) aimed at the sphere, first interaction always a photo absorption
# A narrow beam has (almost) the same path for all photons, thus the weights are (almost) identical
# and unweighted distributions are already correct. For extended beams always use the weight!

Run MyForcedRun
MyForcedRun.FileName                      ForcedFirstInteraction
MyForcedRun.Events                        10000

MyForcedRun.Source MyForcedSource
MyForcedSource.ParticleType               1
MyForcedSource.Beam                       HomogeneousBeam  0 0 90  0 0 -1  0.1
MyForcedSource.Spectrum                   Mono 10000.0
MyForcedSource.Flux                       1.0
MyForcedSource.ForceFirstInteraction      PHOT
